sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-19-conus-second-assessor-audit-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation — Reproducibility package: 78/100" ;
        rdfs:comment "requirements.txt gives lower bounds and requirements.lock.txt gives exact pins with Python 3.14.7, platform and date; every RNG is seeded (42, 17, 100+idx) and no wall clock or unseeded randomness is used. I re-ran the script from the worktree in about 35 s and all five artefacts (two CSVs, two PNGs, GIF) were byte-identical to the shipped ones, which is the strongest possible determinism evidence. The fixture is verified at load and the run works offline. Deductions: the README's documented invocation is wrong, since --no-photos and --no-anim do not exist (argparse exits 2) and --self-test only works through argparse prefix abbreviation of --self-test-only (deduction 12). There is no regeneration path for the specimen-derived fixture, so the input side of the package is not reproducible (deduction 6). No test runner or CI hook wraps the self-test, and matplotlib emits cache-directory warnings when HOME is not writable (deduction 4). Evidence: requirements.lock.txt L1–L10: Exact pip freeze pins with interpreter version, platform and date <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/requirements.lock.txt#L1-L10>; 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L1507–L1514: Actual flags are --no-gif/--self-test-only/--download/--frames/--fps; README documents --self-test, --no-photos, --no-anim <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L1507-L1514>; 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py L155–L158: Seeded default_rng throughout; outputs byte-identical on re-run <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/fb234bc/1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py#L155-L158>; conus_textile_rule30_comparison.png (generated output, not in repo): SHA-256 identical before and after my regeneration — conus_textile_rule30_comparison.png: rendered output of 1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py at fb234bc, image/png, 611089 B, 2640×1632 px, artifact_sha256 b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41 (sha256 b204b836cd08e75a085169a5eb32b8069015a423668ea8a4963f251c1d130e41), spec_fingerprint 6baf9ffa515c0c89775df3b58f398571f7894e64d20534778dff610ad08bc313." ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-repro-package> ;
        pk:hasProbability "0.78"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30-repro-package> rdfs:label "Wolfram (1984) Rule 30 & Meinhardt–Klingler (1987) Conus textile Pigmentation (1984-wolfram-conus-textile-rule30.py, docs/media/conus_textile_rule30.gif, docs/media/conus_rule30_kymograph_defect_fronts.png, conus_textile_rule30_metrics.csv, conus_rule30_defect_fronts.csv) satisfies the MorphoEval 0.1.0 criterion 'Reproducibility package' for Conus textile Linnaeus, 1758 (textile cone snail)" ;
        dct:identifier "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Cursor agent, blinded second assessor)" .
}

